  "period_note": "Year-end position from NRB Bank Limited's own FY2019 Annual Report: Balance Sheet ('Balance Sheet AS AT 31 DECEMBER 2019', Total Assets 54,722,974,357 at line ~5796), Profit and Loss Account (Interest income 4,603,332,997 onward, line ~5860), and the five-year 'Financial Highlights' style table for Capital Adequacy (CRAR 13.32%, Tier-2 1.24%, Tier-1 backed out as CRAR-Tier2=12.08%, matching the FY2023 report's five-year table exactly). All Balance Sheet and P&L figures cross-checked as stable against the FY2020 report's comparative column (exact match to the taka). DATA-QUALITY NOTE (applies to FY2015-FY2022 generally, recorded here once): the 'General provision' / 'Specific provision' figures shown in the FY2015-FY2018 report vintages' five-year summary tables are cumulative BALANCE-SHEET provision-maintained figures, NOT the current year's P&L provision EXPENSE (e.g. FY2019's own P&L shows a General provision *expense* of 75.09m and Specific provision *expense* of 814.08m for the year, which reconcile to the closing balance-sheet provision stock of ~348m/1,110m only after adding the FY2018 opening stock) -- the two concepts share near-identical labels in the source but are not the same number, and are easy to conflate. This dataset does not carry a separate 'provision_maintained' line item for NRBBANK because the balance-figure definition itself appears to have been redefined/regrouped between the FY2016-2018 and FY2019+ report vintages (e.g. FY2016's own five-year table shows FY2015 general provision = 35m, but the FY2018/FY2019 vintages restate the same FY2015 figure to 100m, a ~186% change, with no separate 'specific' balance shown in the earlier vintages at all) -- rather than pick one, this is flagged here as an unresolved sourcing ambiguity in the underlying reports themselves.",
